# Links excluded from the weekly lychee check.
# Regex, one per line. These are NOT broken — they block automated checkers.
#
# Keep this list minimal: every rule here is a link nobody will ever be
# warned about. Add one only with a measured reason, and remove it when the
# link it covers leaves the README.

# Measured from a real request: returns 999 (LinkedIn's anti-bot status)
https://in\.linkedin\.com/.*

# Streamlit Community Cloud redirects every non-browser client to its auth
# endpoint (303 -> share.streamlit.io/-/auth/app), regardless of whether the
# app is public. Verified against Streamlit's own public demos — 30days,
# roadmap and gallery all return 303 too. Real browsers load these fine.
https://.*\.streamlit\.app.*
